### 5.1.7 Technology Selection Justification

The technology stack was selected based on the functional and technical requirements of PortfolioGenie.

The use of React.js supports the development of reusable and interactive user interfaces. Node.js and Express.js provide a flexible backend environment for handling application logic and API communication.

MongoDB offers a flexible document-based data model that can accommodate the different structures of developer profiles, projects, and portfolio configurations.

The integration of GitHub REST API enables automated retrieval of available repository information, while the external AI API provides intelligent content generation capabilities.

Additionally, the use of JavaScript across the frontend and backend simplifies development and improves consistency within the project.

Together, these technologies provide a suitable foundation for developing PortfolioGenie as a maintainable and extensible web application.

### 5.1.8 Conclusion

The selected technology stack provides the essential technical foundation for PortfolioGenie. It supports the development of an interactive frontend, a backend responsible for application logic, a database for persistent data storage, and external integrations for GitHub data retrieval and AI-powered content generation.

The combination of these technologies enables the system to deliver its main objective: simplifying the process of creating professional developer portfolios through automation, customization, and artificial intelligence.
